for the past few months I've been asking  strangers to call their crush and ask  them out on a date for my project series  and so I thought it was time for me to  do the same but before we get there  there are a few things I want to tell  you about this person it's sort of a  complicated love story and as is the  case with most complicated stories there  is a seemingly simple beginning so let's  start there  the Damian this person met was a big  blur there was a lot happening and there  was a lot of people around it's kind of  like one of those memories you only have  because of photos but even if I did  remember I really don't think there was  much to it it was just a simple  acknowledgement that this person now  existed a few years passed before I saw  this person again this memory I  definitely remember and I'm sorry to  tell you this but despite all the fairy  tales you might have heard it was not  love at first sight because the love  this great doesn't start off that easy  it was I saw this person and it felt as  though our worlds collided it wasn't the  kind of collision to ask for attention  it was subtle it was silent  it was the meeting of colors the only we  could see  and has scared the crap out of me so I  made it stomp instead of seeing the good  the potential and how I could fall in  love with this person instead of doing  all of that I decided to make our  relationship complicated despite all  this as time went on I grew closer to  this person  we never formally agreed to be best  friends but the fact is that we were I  grew to learn this person's flaws things  that could get under their skin will  made them sad will made them cry but  more importantly over time I realized  how relentlessly beautiful this person  is how strong they are for putting up  with me for all these years how  resilient they are for forgiving me as  many times as they have without letting  it permanently scar them and how kind  they are for still despite everything  seeing the good and me and so not too  long ago I finally decided I didn't want  things to be complicated between us  anymore  but as is the case with most complicated  stories there is no clearly defined and  so let's cut to now 28 years into my  lifelong love story if you haven't  figured it out by now the person I've  been talking about is me I'm sorry if  you feel that I misled you but I hope  you're happy that I misled you here to a  place where I get the message of loving  yourself across I just feel like we  spend so much time emphasizing that it's  okay to talk about our struggles that  we've lost sight of making it okay to  express our accomplishments most  importantly that it's okay to express  love for oneself as a valid form of love  just as important if not more so  there for as long as I can remember my  relationship with myself has been  complicated but in 2018 I decided to let  go of my fears and uncomplicate things I  know that a lot of people get to this  point of self love in their life but I  feel so lucky that I was able to get to  this point with you all after years of  searching this year I found my purpose  and you all told me it was real so thank  you again a thousand times for helping  me and complicate these  [Music]  [Music]
 

